WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:07.059
India became the world's first nation to reach the South pole of the moon.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.399
On August 20.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.710
India is now on the moon.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.680
Mission control erupted in cheers as the Chan Tayan three landed in a part 

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:22.469
of the moon where no country has ever landed before.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.170
For India.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.610
It's a matter of national pride.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.059
It happened just three days after a similar mission from Russia failed.

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:34.689
It's a blow to the Kremlin because they are trying to show through this mission that 

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.939
Russia is again a superpower.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:42.060
The lunar South Pole is significant because the expected presence of ice could support 

00:00:42.069 --> 00:00:43.779
future human settlements.

00:00:44.319 --> 00:00:49.130
Here's why Moscow and New Delhi were in a race to get there and how their missions were not 

00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:52.549
just about science but also about politics.

00:00:57.119 --> 00:01:02.110
India's Chandra three which means moon vehicle in Sanskrit blasted off from 

00:01:02.119 --> 00:01:03.599
earth on July 14th.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:05.699
Since then,

00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:10.580
the spacecraft made several maneuvers around the earth and has been orbiting the moon to prepare 

00:01:10.589 --> 00:01:11.510
for a landing.

00:01:14.059 --> 00:01:17.940
Russia launched its lunar 25 less than a month later,

00:01:18.319 --> 00:01:23.309
it took a much faster and more direct route to the moon and was projected to reach the 

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:28.139
surface first on August 21 the South Pole is strategic 

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.580
because the expected presence of ice could provide fuel oxygen and drinking 

00:01:32.589 --> 00:01:33.209
water,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.110
making it a potential site for mining and human settlements.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.080
But experts say a smooth landing is extremely challenging.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:46.040
That's because the area has much tougher terrain compared to other parts of the moon.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:50.089
It is bumpy littered with craters and has limited sunlight.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.879
The module has begun its descent.

00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:57.739
India tried but failed to reach there four years ago and finally succeeded 

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.000
on August 23.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.029
This success belongs to all 

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.869
of humanity and it will help 

00:02:12.809 --> 00:02:17.679
by other countries in the future that makes India the 

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:22.309
fourth country in the world to reach the moon after the United States.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.649
Russia and China.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.360
India is expected to get a lot of offers from other space agencies,

00:02:28.369 --> 00:02:32.059
foreign countries to launch commercial satellites for them,

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.500
which is going to be also a revenue earner for India.

00:02:38.229 --> 00:02:42.360
A happy landing for Russia's unmanned lunar 17 spacecraft.

00:02:42.369 --> 00:02:47.000
Russia was the first country to send a rover to the moon back in 1970 

00:02:47.009 --> 00:02:51.899
towards the end of a space race between the US and the Soviet Union during the Cold 

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:52.369
War.

00:02:52.809 --> 00:02:57.729
But Russia hasn't launched another lunar lander since the 19 seventies and the stakes this 

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.820
time around were especially high.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:03.610
More than 18 months after it launched the invasion of Ukraine.

00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:08.335
Western sanctions imposed on Russia since the war complicated its 

00:03:08.345 --> 00:03:12.755
collaborations in space with Europe and the US because of Western 

00:03:12.764 --> 00:03:13.684
sanctions.

00:03:13.695 --> 00:03:18.324
A lot of the cooperation that used to take part in terms of space 

00:03:18.335 --> 00:03:19.175
projects,

00:03:19.235 --> 00:03:20.904
they have come to an end.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:25.494
And also because of technology export bans Russia cannot 

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:30.294
receive a lot of the electronics and other technology that it would have in the past from 

00:03:30.304 --> 00:03:33.625
European nations that supported its space program.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:37.970
So this is extremely significant for India.

00:03:37.979 --> 00:03:42.979
There are political and financial reasons driving its mission to the Lunar South Pole.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:48.380
The successful mission could boost Prime Minister Narendra Modi's election campaign early 

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:49.110
next year.

00:03:49.289 --> 00:03:51.940
These kind of missions adds to the national pride.

00:03:51.949 --> 00:03:56.820
Prime Minister Modi is going to tell his voters how the country 

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:00.220
has reached the moon and which would make to his benefit.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:05.320
The Indian Space Agency works on a shoestring budget in February,

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:09.610
the government slashed funding for the Department of Space by 8% to 

00:04:09.619 --> 00:04:11.679
$1.5 billion.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.020
In comparison,

00:04:13.029 --> 00:04:17.600
nasa's budget for 2023 is more than $25 billion.

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:23.320
India is hoping to get a lot of foreign collaborations in terms of like offers for 

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:26.559
joint venture missions to launch commercial satellites.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.950
So it relies on these foreign collaborations to support its space missions.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:38.040
India's successful landing on the Lunar South Pole could change its standing in the 

00:04:38.049 --> 00:04:39.309
global space race,

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.980
especially in Asia.

00:04:41.299 --> 00:04:45.970
India's position as a global space power would definitely be reinforced.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:50.940
It definitely puts India ahead of countries like Japan and Korea 

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:55.540
and just behind China meanwhile,

00:04:55.549 --> 00:04:59.315
Russia still has a way to go to catch up with the US and China,

00:04:59.394 --> 00:05:01.934
it's not the be all and end all for Russia.

00:05:01.945 --> 00:05:05.744
There are other lunar lunar 26 and lunar 27.

00:05:05.755 --> 00:05:08.875
They both depend on electronics from the West.

00:05:08.885 --> 00:05:11.144
And for as long as sanctions continue,

00:05:11.154 --> 00:05:16.144
it's going to be difficult for Russia to obtain the kind of technology that it needs to 

00:05:16.154 --> 00:05:21.135
continue collaborating and ensuring that it is number one as it 

00:05:21.144 --> 00:05:23.184
wants to be in the space race.

